# Copy to local/opnsense-api.env (gitignored) OR generate it with:
#   scripts/opnsense.sh --import ~/Downloads/<hostname>_agent_apikey.txt
#
# OPNsense 25.7 keypair creation (verified against the 25.7 source):
#   1. System > Access > Users > + : user "nate", a password,
#      group "admins" (do NOT hang keys off root)
#   2. On the USERS LIST (not the edit dialog): at the right end of the
#      nate row, click the row's command icons -- the one titled
#      "Create and download API key for this user" (ticket-style icon)
#   3. Confirm "Generate and download API key?" -> the browser downloads
#      <hostname>_agent_apikey.txt containing "key=..." and "secret=..."
#   4. scripts/opnsense.sh --import <that file>  (chmod 600, then
#      sanity-checks the connection)
# NEVER commit this file; never paste the secret into chat -- this file
# is the only place it lives. The keypair is revocable on its own
# without touching any human account.
OPNSENSE_HOST=192.168.1.1
OPNSENSE_KEY=paste-nate-api-key-here
OPNSENSE_SECRET=paste-nate-api-secret-here
